From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Justin Walsh <contact.me@thejustinwalsh.com>
Date: Sun, 28 Sep 2026 09:00:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] moe expert cache: Strata's expert profile, its adaptive tier,
 and every CPU-computed batch

Strata code in this patch: Copyright (c) 2026 Niko1221 and the Strata contributors, MIT License
(LICENSE added in Strata c0107c3, blob 6687a423dde6b7aff1b748c07f5ee93ff788089c; the full notice is
engines/patches/llama-upstream-flash/LICENSE.strata). First ported from d551edf4 on 2026-09-28, before the
licence, on the operator's authorisation; re-attributed 2026-09-29 against 3ce2523c, where every cited
piece still stands under MIT.

On top of 0003 (PR #27861's mechanism). Ported from Strata, credit Niko1221:

- LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_PROFILE=<STRP file>: the resident experts are chosen from
  an expert profile, Strata's format and reader (src/core/expert_cache.cpp:
  12-72 read_expert_profile; data/expert-profile.bin; tools/make_profile.py).
  The cache takes n_slots x (host-resident expert layers) pairs in rank
  order, so each layer gets as many slots as the ranking gives it, and they
  are filled before the first decode (Strata's blocking startup fill,
  include/strata/core/expert_cache.hpp:112-118). A layer given no slot is
  not cached.
- LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_POLICY=strata: promotions at deliberate moments --
  Strata's adaptive tier (src/program/generate.cpp:2418-2457; usage counted
  per routed id at src/core/expert_source.cpp:275-277): every
  LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_ADAPT_EVERY steps (its --adapt-every 4, generate.cpp:246)
  and only when the previous swaps have landed, per layer the missing experts
  with usage >= 2 replace the least-used resident ones while the gain is
  >= 1.5, the best LLAMA_MOE_CACHE_ADAPT_SWAPS (its --adapt-swaps 96, :258)
  overall; the victim is evicted at once (the CPU computes it meanwhile), the
  newcomer admitted when its copy lands; then usage *= 0.7 (:2456). Default
  stays #27861's LRU.
- Generalised beyond one token: the cache chain is built for every batch the
  CPU computes, n_tokens < ggml-cuda's op-offload batch
  (GGML_OP_OFFLOAD_MIN_BATCH, default 32), so MTP verify windows and several
  slots decoding together are served (Strata serves its verify windows the
  same way). Above that batch the op runs on the GPU with the experts copied
  in, and the skip table would not be honoured, so the chain is not built.

Any MoE model whose experts are separate gate/up/down with SiLU (the scope
of #27861) benefits; the profile is per model (a Flash-Next profile is
Strata's data/expert-profile.bin, 48 x 512; scripts/moe_profile.py builds
one for any model from GGML_MOE_LOG traces).
